# Issue #104: path membership survives rewiring to a replacement group:
# cd (rewired G -> D) is a path flow and stays; db (rewired D -> G) is
# downstream of D, off the upstream paths, and is hidden.

process A
process B
process C
process D
process G Group

A -> B ab
B -> C bc
C -> D cd
D -> B db

!!<2 D G
merge B C : G
